{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The U.S. should work with the international community to cut off funds to the I.S. by cracking down on Turkish, Iraqi and other oil dealers who purchase I.S. oil on the black market.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Saudi Arabia and the Gulf States largely own the banks in Northern Iraq through which the I.S. washes its funds.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The United States coddles the repressive Gulf States because of the U.S.'s desire to have access to their oil.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"In order to cut off funds to the political Islamists, the United States government must definitively break with the repressive Gulf States.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The repressive Gulf States fund both the political Islamist forces and the Wahabist religious schools that provide the ideological underpinning for reactionary political Islamists.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The United States must press its NATO ally Turkey to grant greater autonomy and freedom to its Kurdish population.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The United States must press its NATO ally Turkey to open a corridor from Turkey for arms and Kurdish reinforcements to reach the besieged Syrian Kurdish fighters in Kobani.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The United States should provide incentives for Turkey to grant greater autonomy and freedom to its Kurdish population and to open a corridor from Turkey for arms and Kurdish reinforcements by increasing humanitarian aid to the displaced people from both Syria and Iraq flooding into Turkish refugee camps.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

